     "bbox": [
      314.64,
      84.24,
      549.36,
      93.96
     ],
     "text": "\u2018Taranna\u2019 is a perennial grass native to Australia and so should"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      314.28,
      95.4,
      549.36,
      105.12
     ],
     "text": "be adapted to dry conditions and low soil fertility. It is intended"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      313.92,
      106.56,
      549.72,
      116.28
     ],
     "text": "for use in temperate areas either for aerial establishment into"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      314.28,
      118.08,
      549.72,
      127.08
     ],
     "text": "non-arable, hilly country or as a pasture grass in degraded crop-"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      314.28,
      129.6,
      550.08,
      138.96
     ],
     "text": "ping lands. It produces more growth in spring, early-summer"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      314.28,
      140.76,
      503.28,
      149.4
     ],
     "text": "than \u2018Hume\u2019 and has a high rate of seed retention."
    }
   ],
   "page": 1,
   "source": "tesseract-psm3",
   "text": "\u2018Taranna\u2019 is a perennial grass native to Australia and so should\nbe adapted to dry conditions and low soil fertility. It is intended\nfor use in temperate areas either for aerial establishment into\nnon-arable, hilly country or as a pasture grass in degraded crop-\nping lands. It produces more growth in spring, early-summer\nthan \u2018Hume\u2019 and has a high rate of seed retention.",
   "text_format": "plain",
   "type": "text"
  },
